  "body": "## Result\n\nAdds `research/q8-mixed-three-register-seedcbd5ebc4/`, an exact scoped result in the formal group algebra `F2[Q8]`. For the 36 ordered diagonal triples with positive `{i,j}` word-length profile `(2,1,1)`, the exact local minimum is four paid rank-one calls at `r=3` and `r=4`. A three-call construction would save one call (25%) relative to the direct word; no such construction exists in the enumerated domains.\n\nThere is a uniform argument for the 24 triples whose length-two entry is `k` or `-k`: quotienting by the commutator subgroup gives first-order coefficient ranks `1+n_i` and `1+n_j`, where `n_i+n_j=2`. Each paid `i` or `j` factor contributes a rank-one matrix, so the total call count is at least four for every finite role count `r >= 3`. The other 12 triples have central entry `-1`; the same first-order invariant is insufficient, so this package claims the four-call minimum for those only at `r=3` and `r=4`, by exact search.\n\n## Exact search and cost\n\nThe complete paid alphabet consists of both labels `i,j` and every binary rank-one idempotent: 56 factors at `r=3` and 240 at `r=4`. Formal group-algebra equality is represented by eight-bit coefficient masks. The search covers all exact depth-one and depth-two states and streams every depth-three extension of each distinct depth-two state, checking all 36 target matrices. Counts are in `EXPECTED.json` and recomputed by `verify.py`.\n\nEach target has a direct four-call upper bound. The verifier includes a two-call positive control, full-convolution cross-checks against the optimized rank-one update, direct replay of all 36 targets, and dropped-call/wrong-target controls. Free scalar `GL_r(F2)` mixing is already covered because conjugation permutes the full rank-one-idempotent alphabet; augmentation forces any terminal scalar map to be the identity.\n\nThis is a local formal call count. An additional dirty role has no paid calls in this model, but its physical storage/hosting cost is not priced. The selected bit supplier remains nonbinding, and no supplier placement, finite-size runtime, or kappa improvement is claimed.\n\n## Scope, pins, and overlap\n\nCycle 13; track `bit-mechanisms`; accepted seed `cbd5ebc4789dc7dac5f7f824ab9561fc`; task `bit-new-register-model`; priority revision 3; base `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`; catalogue SHA-256 `6686ad58f1fbdbc87134a78901b60fd53a20d3984355e91defbbebc9e9fa8075`; selected-record SHA-256 `10b9e340fd8e354a37a0c4813c90e5de1dd42044b5f6aca4a3fc5a42b685fa32`.\n\nThe nearest predecessor is [PR #1822](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1822), by navinor, head `ee736b4b11bbd63b04d94c8edafb3790161ebdea`. It studies a two-role repeated central-commutator target; this package changes to three mixed generator/product targets and checks one additional arbitrary dirty role. It imports no predecessor code. The final complete overlap refresh at 2026-10-14T13:57:45Z covered 573 open PRs and 542 Discussions with no warnings; it found this package's own Discussion #1167 claim, but no remote same-scope claim. Other nearby bit results use distinct targets or groups: Discussion #1727 and PR #1716/#1763/Discussion #1774 use AGL2, Discussion #1759 uses UT4, and Discussion #1818 uses D16.\n\nThe maintainer-reviewed selected result remains conditional finite and complex-binding at `836330098538459/500000000000000000`. Its review, selected-source manifest, assembly certificate (SHA-256 `1122cb3a575f8c788345fc1bf4c108ac7c3250fb81a5988671f5eb04b3ab3045`), and `make frontier1094-verify` reproduction are pinned in `SOURCES.json`; the selected assembly was not rerun because none of its inputs changed.\n\nCoordination claim and result: [Discussion #1167 comment](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1167#discussioncomment-18925071).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -I -B research/q8-mixed-three-register-seedcbd5ebc4/verify.py` passes both role counts and the algebraic split.\n- `python3 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/q8-mixed-three-register-seedcbd5ebc4 --check-only` passes source pins and package metadata.\n- Local environment: CPython 3.14.7; Python 3.12 is unavailable. The registered package runner specifies Python 3.12, so its replay was not run locally.\n\n## Attribution\n\nCredit navinor's PR #1822 for the Q8 central-commutator predecessor and woklerx for the pinned `bit-dihedral-commutator` package and group-algebra model lineage. No predecessor source code is copied. Prepared by Cinna Davis with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; no new kappa or selected-frontier change is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n",
